; The registry gala boots with: the keys and values real programs read,
; with the values Windows 11 24H2 (build 26100) has, adapted to gala's
; machine (user gala, computer GALA, code page UTF-8). Loaded by
; nt::registry::load into memory at boot.
;
; Format: [\Registry\...] starts a key (made with any missing parents);
; "name"=type:data or @=type:data (the unnamed value) sets a value. Types:
; sz, expand (REG_EXPAND_SZ), multi (items separated by |), dword, qword
; (decimal or 0x hex), hex (bytes, comma-separated). Data runs to the end
; of the line, backslashes as they are. Lines starting ; are comments.

[\Registry\Machine\HARDWARE\DESCRIPTION\System]
[\Registry\Machine\SAM]
[\Registry\Machine\SECURITY]

; Windows 11 still reports itself as "Windows 10" in ProductName (and
; CurrentVersion 6.3); programs tell Windows 11 by CurrentBuild >= 22000.
[\Registry\Machine\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion]
"ProductName"=sz:Windows 10 Pro
"EditionID"=sz:Professional
"InstallationType"=sz:Client
"CurrentVersion"=sz:6.3
"CurrentBuild"=sz:26100
"CurrentBuildNumber"=sz:26100
